---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "") + "/";
const image = (name: string) => base + "figures/" + name;
const extraModels = [
  { name: "Qwen3-8B", before: [63, 38, 53, 90], after: [1, 0, 3, 5] },
  { name: "Llama2-13B-chat", before: [14, 16, 17, 18], after: [1, 0, 0, 0] },
  {
    name: "Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct",
    before: [69, 42, 68, 93],
    after: [3, 0, 5, 3],
  },
];
---

<div class="results-supporting">
  <details class="evidence-details">
    <summary
      ><span>Do edits transfer across harmful behaviors?</span><span
        >Figure 6</span
      ></summary
    ><div class="details-body">
      <p>
        We edit one HarmBench behavior category at a time and evaluate all six
        categories. The heatmaps show that targeted edits can also reduce attack
        success on categories not used for editing.
      </p>
      <div class="ablation-figures">
        <figure>
          <img
            src={image("delman-transfer-gcg.png")}
            alt="Llama2-7B cross-category attack success after a single-category edit under GCG."
            width="3319"
            height="2454"
            loading="lazy"
          /><figcaption>Llama2-7B-chat · GCG</figcaption>
        </figure><figure>
          <img
            src={image("delman-transfer-autodan.png")}
            alt="Llama2-7B cross-category attack success after a single-category edit under AutoDAN."
            width="3319"
            height="2454"
            loading="lazy"
          /><figcaption>Llama2-7B-chat · AutoDAN</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <p class="table-note">
        Columns denote editing categories, and rows denote evaluated categories.
        Off-diagonal cells show transfer to other categories. Original ASR
        values appear in parentheses. ASR is shown on a 0–1 scale (lower is
        better).
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>
  <details class="evidence-details">
    <summary
      ><span>What do harmful key representations show?</span><span
        >Figure 7</span
      ></summary
    ><div class="details-body">
      <p>
        PCA projections of harmful keys at the selected editing layer show
        substantial overlap across behavior categories and datasets. This
        suggests shared representation patterns among harmful inputs.
      </p>
      <div class="ablation-figures">
        <figure>
          <img
            src={image("delman-keys-behaviors.png")}
            alt="PCA projections of harmful token keys, colored by behavior category."
            width="3453"
            height="3363"
            loading="lazy"
          /><figcaption>Across harmful behaviors</figcaption>
        </figure><figure>
          <img
            src={image("delman-keys-datasets.png")}
            alt="PCA projections of harmful token keys, colored by dataset."
            width="3453"
            height="3363"
            loading="lazy"
          /><figcaption>Across datasets</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </details>
  <details class="evidence-details">
    <summary
      ><span>Additional models and scales</span><span>Table 9</span></summary
    ><div class="details-body">
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table class="result-table">
          <thead
            ><tr
              ><th scope="col">Model</th><th scope="col">Method</th>{
                [
                  "HarmBench",
                  "AdvBench",
                  "JailbreakBench",
                  "MaliciousInstruct",
                ].map((name) => <th scope="col">{name}</th>)
              }</tr
            ></thead
          ><tbody
            >{
              extraModels.map((model) => (
                <>
                  <>
                    <tr>
                      <th scope="rowgroup" rowspan="2">
                        {model.name}
                      </th>
                      <th scope="row">Original Model</th>
                      {model.before.map((value) => (
                        <td>{value}%</td>
                      ))}
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="delman-row">
                      <th scope="row">DELMAN</th>
                      {model.after.map((value) => (
                        <td>
                          <strong>{value}%</strong>
                        </td>
                      ))}
                    </tr>
                  </>
                </>
              ))
            }</tbody
          >
        </table>
      </div><p class="table-note">
        GCG attack success rate (ASR, %), lower is better.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>
</div>
